And now Pope Leo XIV is talking about this again because this is the new industrial revolution, but it's the information revolution in which the dignity of the worker and work itself is sort of under threat in a way by this machine that is able to replicate a lot of the intellectual labor that we've come to take on as human beings and I don't know I haven't sorted all this out yet but you know I think about the liberal arts and I think about why they're called the liberal arts and they were freedom from manual labor and now are we saying that we're going to give the machine this sort of activity this mental activity that we think being our own freedom the way that we can think freely about things and come to know the world and so I think In that way, AI is different because it is extending a human faculty that's.

